# evidence/.gitkeep
# =============================================================================
# This directory stores all FORENSIC EVIDENCE packages.
# Evidence packages are grouped by scan_id — one subdirectory per scan.
# =============================================================================
#
# FUTURE DIRECTORY STRUCTURE:
#
#   evidence/
#   ├── SCAN-550e8400/
#   │   └── evidence-EV-abc12345.json     — Forensic evidence package for this scan
#   │
#   ├── SCAN-a1b2c3d4/
#   │   └── evidence-EV-def67890.json
#   │
#   └── SCAN-ff001122/
#       └── evidence-EV-ghi11223.json
#
# FORENSIC EVIDENCE PACKAGE (per scan):
#   Each evidence-<evidence_id>.json file contains the COMPLETE forensic record
#   for a single scan run:
#     - scan_id                   — Unique Scan ID for this pipeline run
#     - repository_url            — URL of the scanned repository
#     - commit_sha                — Exact git commit SHA scanned
#     - scan_metadata             — Full scan context record
#     - terraform_discovery       — All discovered Terraform modules
#     - checkov_findings          — All static IaC findings
#     - policy_violations         — All OPA/Rego policy violations
#     - runtime_findings          — All Prowler runtime findings
#     - static_risk_score         — Initial risk score
#     - final_risk_score          — Combined risk score and trust score
#     - final_decision            — ALLOW / REVIEW / BLOCK
#     - evidence_id               — Unique identifier for this evidence package
#     - evidence_hash             — SHA256 integrity hash of the complete package
#
# CHAIN OF CUSTODY:
#   Repository URL → Clone → Scan ID → All findings → Decision → Evidence
#   Every link is captured, timestamped, and hashed for forensic integrity.
#
# All JSON evidence files are excluded from Git via .gitignore.
# Only this .gitkeep file is tracked by Git.
# =============================================================================
